This code provides the basic framework for a modular, efficient C++ library for real-time data streaming processing. It includes classes to represent data sources, processors, aggregators, sinks, and a main function to start processing data streams.

The DataEvent class represents a data event with an ID and data.
The DataSource class is an abstract base class that provides a way to get the next available data event from the source.
The DataProcessor class is a thread-based class that processes data events from multiple sources in parallel. The run function starts processing data events, and the start function starts the processor.
The DataAggregator class is a thread-based class that aggregates data events. It provides an override for the processNextEvent function to aggregate data events and send them to a destination or perform further processing.
The DataSink class is an abstract base class that provides a way to process the next available data event from the queue.
The DataSourceAggregator class aggregates data events from multiple sources.
The DataStreamProcessor class processes data events from multiple sources.
The DataStreamSink class sends processed data to a destination or performs further processing.

This library can be extended to handle high-throughput data streams, scalable event aggregation and transformation, performance optimization, and resource management.']

